{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01FNgeFfsXTSefF3iZ4XSEUX","type":"tool_result","content":"src/lib.rs == pre-mutation state (clean)\n--- final lib.rs body ---\n/// void gaussian_kernel(float *dest, int size, float radius);\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn gaussian_kernel(dest: *mut f32, size: c_int, radius: f32) {\n    let sigma: f32 = 1.6f32;\n    let tetha: f32 = 2.25f32;\n    let hsize: c_int = size / 2;\n\n    let s2: f32 = 1.0f32 / expf(sigma * sigma * tetha);\n    let rs: f32 = sigma / radius;\n\n    let mut k: *mut f32 = dest;\n    let mut sum: f32 = 0.0f32;\n\n    let mut r: c_int = -hsize;\n    while r <= hsize {\n        let x: f32 = (r as f32) * rs;\n        let mut v: f32 = (1.0f32 / expf(x * x)) - s2;\n        // C: v = ((v) > (0)) ? (v) : (0);  -- integer 0 promotes to 0.0f\n        v = if v > 0.0f32 { v } else { 0.0f32 };\n        // C dereferences a plain `float *`; on the target ABI that is a single\n        // `movss`, which tolerates unaligned addresses. Use unaligned accesses\n        // so an unaligned `dest` behaves exactly like the C build instead of\n        // tripping Rust's debug-only alignment assertion.\n        k.write_unaligned(v);\n        sum += v;\n        k = k.add(1);\n        r += 1;\n    }\n\n    if sum > 0.0f32 {\n        let isum: f32 = 1.0f32 / sum;\n        let mut r: c_int = 0;\n        while r < size {\n            let p = dest.offset(r as isize);\n            p.write_unaligned(p.read_unaligned() * isum);\n            r += 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n--- artifacts ---\n  100 SYMBOLS.md\n   59 ERRORS.md\n   60 CONFIGS.md\n 1117 tests/differential.rs\n   72 run_verification.sh\n 1408 total\n12:libloading = \"0.8\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78ad3e7d-e8ec-4d1d-962b-cc334325ed55","uuid":"439bc487-540c-455f-b66e-8cc032a5c8b9","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:33:49.104Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"src/lib.rs == pre-mutation state (clean)\n--